      "description": "Watch Austria vs Israel highlights and goals from UEFA Nations League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 24, 2026. A hard-fought battle under the lights On September 24, 2026 , the UEFA Nations League witnessed a compelling encounter as Austria hosted Israel . The match was defined by physical intensity and tactical maneuvering, as both sides looked to seize control of the midfield battle throughout a cagey opening half. The momentum shift Austria took the initiative just before halftime when Romano Schmid coolly converted a penalty after a foul by Idan Nachmias on Sasa Kalajdzic . The game exploded into life in the second half when Sayed Abu Farkhi leveled for Israel with a powerful header. However, the joy was short-lived as Abu Farkhi was sent off for a second yellow card shortly after his celebration, leaving his team vulnerable against a revitalized Austrian side. Late drama secures the points As the clock ticked toward full-time, Austria turned the screw on the 10-man Israeli defense. The breakthrough arrived in the 90th minute when Phillipp Mwene fired home from a Paul Wanner assist. With the tension at its peak in front of the 15,200 spectators, Sasa Kalajdzic hammered home the final goal in stoppage time, assisted by Christoph Lang , to cement a hard-earned 3-1 victory."
